+  // ---- Phase 2 (plane split): composite the OVER plane above the weave ----
+  //
+  // This is the consumer patch 0063 built the plane for, and the whole point of
+  // --inline-3d-occlusion: without it the page buries the tile, because the
+  // page raster is painted first and the woven tile is drawn back over it. With
+  // it, SkiaRenderer has (a) punched every over-tile quad OUT of the page
+  // raster (the kDifference clip, live as of this patch) and (b) painted those
+  // quads into |inline_3d_over_plane_mailbox_|, a window-sized premul RGBA8
+  // plane that is transparent everywhere except inside the tile rects. Drawing
+  // it kSrcOver right after the woven draw-back is what puts that content back
+  // ON TOP.
+  //
+  // The per-pixel contract inside a tile rect, in the order it is established:
+  //   1. |output| at the tile rect holds page + under-content only — the
+  //      difference clip removed the over content before phase (A) snapshotted
+  //      it, so the 0050 pre-blend backdrop IS the true backdrop (see the R9
+  //      note there).
+  //   2. the woven draw covers the tile rect OPAQUELY: 0050 pre-blends that
+  //      backdrop under the SBS so the tile leaves the weave with alpha = 1,
+  // and
+  //      the backdrop it pre-blended is exactly output[tile_rect]. So kSrcOver
+  //      and kSrc coincide there and the tile's own pixels win outright.
+  //   3. this plane then composites 2D-over those pixels, per-pixel, with the
+  //      page's own premultiplied alpha — so an opaque element over a tile is
+  //      crisp 2D (no half-width squeeze, no weave lattice) and a translucent
+  //      scrim blends against the woven tile ONCE, not twice.
+  // Outside the tile rects the plane is transparent by construction (the paint
+  // clips every draw into a tile rect), so this whole-window draw cannot touch
+  // 2D chrome elsewhere.
+  //
+  // Partial swap: the plane's clear+paint is bounded by tile_rects ∩ scissor,
+  // so an undamaged region of the plane holds the pixels it held last frame —
+  // and those are identical to what it would repaint, because the page content
+  // that produced them did not change (that is what "undamaged" means).
+  // Sampling the whole window is therefore safe; it is the same contract the
+  // whole-window woven draw above already relies on.
+  //
+  // NOTE the frames where phase (B) bails early (browser#87: nothing wove this
+  // frame, or nothing woven yet): the punched-out content is not restored on
+  // those frames. That is bounded to exactly the tile rects, which are ALREADY
+  // wrong on those frames in Phase 1 too (the canvas resource is suppressed and
+  // nothing is drawn back, so the tile shows bare backdrop) — so no region is
+  // affected that was not already affected. It is not a new artifact class.
+  bool over_plane_drawn = false;
+  bool over_plane_size_ok = false;
+  if (inline3d_occlusion_enabled_ && !inline_3d_over_plane_mailbox_.IsZero()) {
+    // Risk guard R7, as the field's header comment demands: a plane that is not
+    // exactly window-sized would smear if sampled 1:1, so skip rather than
+    // stretch. Transient (one frame after a resize, until the renderer paints a
+    // new plane), hence throttled rather than a one-shot log.
